            "type": "checkpoint",
            "mode": "self_check",
            "ref": "15",
            "prompt": "15. Evaluate \\(\\int \\dfrac{\\tan^{-1}\\sqrt{x}}{\\sqrt{x}}\\,dx\\).",
            "explanation": "The \\(\\sqrt{x}\\) appears twice: substitute \\(t = \\sqrt{x}\\).\nPlan: get \\(2\\int \\tan^{-1}t\\,dt\\), integrate by parts with \\(\\tan^{-1}t\\cdot 1\\).",
            "steps": [
              "Given: \\(\\int \\frac{\\tan^{-1}\\sqrt{x}}{\\sqrt{x}}\\,dx\\), \\(x > 0\\).\nTo find: the indefinite integral.\nMethod: substitute \\(t = \\sqrt{x}\\); then \\(2\\int \\tan^{-1}t\\,dt\\) by parts.",
              "Substitute\n\\[t = \\sqrt{x} \\Rightarrow dt = \\dfrac{1}{2\\sqrt{x}}\\,dx\\]\n\\[\\dfrac{dx}{\\sqrt{x}} = 2\\,dt\\]\n\\[= 2\\int \\tan^{-1}t\\,dt\\]\nWhy: \\(\\frac{d}{dx}\\sqrt{x} = \\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x}}\\).",
              "Parts with \\(\\tan^{-1}t\\cdot 1\\)\n\\[= 2\\left[t\\tan^{-1}t - \\int \\dfrac{t}{1+t^2}\\,dt\\right]\\]\nWhy: \\(\\frac{d}{dt}\\tan^{-1}t = \\frac{1}{1+t^2}\\), \\(\\int 1\\,dt = t\\).",
              "Log integral\n\\[= 2t\\tan^{-1}t - 2\\cdot\\dfrac{1}{2}\\ln(1+t^2) + c\\]\n\\[= 2t\\tan^{-1}t - \\ln(1+t^2) + c\\]\nWhy: \\(\\int \\frac{t}{1+t^2}\\,dt = \\frac{1}{2}\\ln(1+t^2)\\).",
              "Return to \\(x\\)\n\\[= 2\\sqrt{x}\\tan^{-1}\\sqrt{x} - \\ln(1 + x) + c\\]\nWhy: \\(t = \\sqrt{x}\\), \\(t^2 = x\\).",
              "Check\n\\[\\dfrac{d}{dx}(\\ldots) = \\dfrac{\\tan^{-1}\\sqrt{x}}{\\sqrt{x}} + \\dfrac{1}{1+x} - \\dfrac{1}{1+x}\\]\nWhy: \\(\\frac{d}{dx}2\\sqrt{x} = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}\\) and \\(2\\sqrt{x}\\cdot\\frac{1}{1+x}\\cdot\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x}} = \\frac{1}{1+x}\\)."
            ],
            "final_answer": "\\(2\\sqrt{x}\\tan^{-1}\\sqrt{x} - \\ln(1 + x) + c\\)"
          }
        ]
      }
    }
  ]
